# Non-boolean while condition rejected

Verifies a `while` condition must produce the configured boolean type: an
integer literal is rejected before execution with the standard type
diagnostic.

>>> source
while (1) {
    print(1)
}

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: while condition must produce `bool`, found `int64` at Span { start: 7, end: 8 }

<<< exit
1
